@*
    One shape, three registers.

    Neutral for newly discovered, unlit for went dark, and — for a return — the one place the site
    raises its voice. It earns it: a game dark for two years answering again is the thing no
    incumbent can tell you, and it is the whole argument for probing forever instead of giving up.

    The return card gets a full sentence at body size instead of mono metadata, and it is the one
    element allowed motion beyond a disclosure: a single 1.4s glow on arrival, never repeating,
    suppressed entirely under prefers-reduced-motion.
*@

@*
    A row, not a card. Three lists of five boxed cards was three columns of boxes on a page whose
    only other framed thing is a connect screen — and a card per game gives a name, an age and at
    most six words the furniture of a section. Name left, age right, a hairline between: the shape
    the handoff draws, and the shape a list of "what changed" wants.
*@
<article class="feed-row @Register">
    @* Off when the card sits under a column that already names the register, so the page does not
       read "newly discovered newly discovered". A screen reader still gets it: the columns are
       sections labelled by their own heading. *@
    @if (ShowRegister)
    {
        <div class="kicker">@Heading</div>
    }
    <div class="feed-name">
        <a href="/g/@Entry.Slug">@Entry.Name</a>
        @* One cell at the row's right edge: the state, where there is one, and then the age — so a
           returned game reads "live · 4h" rather than dropping its marker onto a line of its own. *@
        <span class="feed-state">
            @if (Kind is FeedKind.CameBack)
            {
                <span class="mono state-present">● live</span>
                <span class="faint" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            }
            <Moment At="Entry.At" Now="Now" Class="mono faint" />
        </span>
    </div>
    @* Only where there is something to add. A row whose detail restated its own column heading was
       one line of repetition per game, and the feeds are ten games deep. *@
    @if (Entry.Detail is { Length: > 0 })
    {
        <p class="@(Kind is FeedKind.CameBack ? "return-line" : "mono detail")">@Entry.Detail</p>
    }
</article>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public FeedEntry Entry { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public FeedKind Kind { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public DateTimeOffset Now { get; set; } = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;

    [Parameter] public bool ShowRegister { get; set; } = true;

    private string Register => Kind switch
    {
        FeedKind.WentDark => "unlit",
        FeedKind.CameBack => "returned",
        _ => "neutral",
    };

    private string Heading => Kind switch
    {
        FeedKind.WentDark => "went dark",
        FeedKind.CameBack => "came back",
        _ => "newly discovered",
    };
}
